cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the PACE toolkit (pace, pace-eval; legacy aliases cme, mae-eval), the extracted contrast datasets, or the hidden-profile control task, please cite the manuscript below."
type: software
title: "PACE: More Agents, More Samples, or More Thinking? Untangling Coordination, Ensembling, and Test-Time Compute in Multi-Agent LLMs"
abstract: "Software, extracted data and analysis code for comparing multi-agent language-model systems with single-agent baselines of different strength: a six-dimension resource vector, a baseline ladder (A single pass, B sampled, C resource-matched, D Pareto frontier), a self-consistency frontier with a paired bootstrap interval, a baseline-rung classifier, a seven-field PACE Evaluation Card, PACE Studio interactive workbench, controlled MMLU-Pro and Hidden Profile experiments, and a synthetic split-evidence positive control."
